{
  "requirement": "For requirement and example evidence, both `true` and `FIXME` MUST satisfy the determination check in `habeas::validate()`. A false determination MUST fail validation and be reported with its rationale. Each definition's determination MUST be checked on its own; a false determination MUST NOT fail the definitions it implements, tests, or cites. All other evidence checks MUST still pass: FIXME MUST NOT excuse malformed, missing, or stale evidence or uncovered references. Validation MUST check the recorded outcome, schema, input freshness, and reference coverage without inference or reassessing whether a source comment adequately acknowledges a gap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the implementation and tests satisfy `requirements.ci.determination`.**\n\n**Implementation**\n- `validate_evidence_file` in `src/evidence.rs` (marked `{impl}`) parses the determination with `Judgment::from_value`. Only `Some(Judgment::False)` produces an error: `\"<record>: determination is false: <trimmed rationale>\"`. `true` and `FIXME` add no error, so they pass the determination check. A false record fails with its rationale reported.\n- The check is per record. It pushes an error only for the record it is reading. Nothing in it looks at that record's `{impl}`, `{test}` or `{cite}` relationships, so a false record cannot fail the definitions it implements, tests or cites.\n- FIXME does not excuse the other checks. All the other checks run whatever the determination is:\n  - schema and shape;\n  - requirement/example text freshness;\n  - the reference-set digest;\n  - input and outline freshness;\n  - dependencies;\n  - missing and orphaned files.\n\n  Reference coverage (\"no input covers …\", anchor coverage and the reference-set check) in `validate_references` also ignores the determination. The one exception is the example `{test}` check, which fires only for `true` (a `true` example needs a `{test}` reference). That exception is the carve-out of `requirements.ci.fixme_example_test_gaps`, not an extra behaviour here.\n- Validation uses only the recorded values. `Judgment::from_value` enforces the FIXME shape. Nothing reads source comments or judges whether a FIXME is adequately acknowledged.\n- `src/citations.rs::validate` is also marked `{impl}`. Its `validate_review` helper applies the same false-fails rule to citation reviews. That goes beyond this requirement's wording, which covers requirement and example evidence. Citation reviews are covered by `requirements.references.citation_review` and `requirements.ci.outcomes`, which that code also marks. The marker on `validate` is slightly loose, because the false check sits in `validate_review`. I do not count it as a gap.\n\n**Tests**\n- `a_false_determination_fails_only_its_own_record_with_its_rationale` (`src/evidence.rs`) uses a false requirement that both `{impl}` and `{cite}` a true one. The only error is the false record's, with the whitespace-trimmed rationale. The implemented and cited record is unaffected.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` shows the false error is reported alongside the other errors, so a false record does not stop later checks.\n- `fixme_examples_pass_without_test_references_but_true_examples_do_not` (`tests/outcomes.rs`) covers an example going `FIXME`, then `true`, then `false`. FIXME passes, `true` without a `{test}` reference fails, and `false` reports \"determination is false\".\n- `fixme_requirements_accept_issue_references_and_other_content` shows FIXME passes both with an issue reference and with free text, backed by a source comment. `fixme_fixture` in `tests/commands.rs` shows it also passes with no comments at all. This is consistent with validation not judging comment adequacy.\n- `fixme_does_not_hide_stale_inputs_or_uncovered_references` shows a FIXME record still fails on a stale input and on an uncovered `{impl}` reference.\n- `malformed_fixme_is_invalid_and_reports_the_required_shape` and `judgments_round_trip_and_reject_invalid_fixme_shapes` show malformed FIXME values are rejected.\n- The authoring-batch tests (`tests/authoring_batch.rs`) show validation passing with a recorded `{\"FIXME\": [\"#123\"]}`. They also show current false judgments are preserved and stale ones are re-authored.\n\nThe tests cover the boundaries: true, false and FIXME, requirement and example, stale and uncovered references, malformed FIXME shapes, and isolation of a false record from the records that implement or cite it. I found no gaps and no acknowledged FIXMEs against this requirement.",
  "references": "7654bcb6b2ec344e3bb41e2d6842db9ad15628cf9a7e6b60a146d2ee61372222",
